WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.055
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:02.055 --> 00:00:03.738
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:03.738 --> 00:00:05.862
My one word is "believe", and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:08.328
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:08.328 --> 00:00:10.373
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.373 --> 00:00:13.189
today's message is "you earn success".

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:15.272
Over to you, Eric Thomas.

00:00:17.561 --> 00:00:19.732
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:22.463
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:22.463 --> 00:00:25.963
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:30.181
- I did not become successful
with two-family household,

00:00:30.181 --> 00:00:32.264
with the income $250,000.

00:00:33.196 --> 00:00:35.808
I was homeless, I was knocked out,

00:00:35.808 --> 00:00:37.442
I was kicked out of school.

00:00:37.442 --> 00:00:39.120
I was told never to return.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.118
I did this in the midst of trials,

00:00:41.118 --> 00:00:43.463
in the midst of tribulations.

00:00:43.463 --> 00:00:45.974
Nobody gave me this, I earned it.

00:00:45.974 --> 00:00:48.094
Life wasn't a crystal stair for me.

00:00:48.094 --> 00:00:49.725
Didn't nobody give me a network.

00:00:49.725 --> 00:00:51.318
I earned a network.

00:00:51.318 --> 00:00:52.911
I know Warren Buffet

00:00:52.911 --> 00:00:54.309
because I worked my way to Warren Buffet.

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:55.897
I worked my way to Dag Gilbert.

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:57.414
I worked my way to the MBA.

00:00:57.414 --> 00:00:59.052
I worked my way to the NFL.

00:00:59.052 --> 00:01:01.181
Everybody say, "E, how'd
you crack the code?"

00:01:01.181 --> 00:01:03.019
I grinded my way through the code.

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:04.655
That's how I cracked it.

00:01:04.655 --> 00:01:06.043
I got up every day at three.

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:09.106
Monday I grind, Tuesday
I grind, Wednesday...

00:01:09.106 --> 00:01:10.617
I don't care what the economy is doing.

00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:12.087
I don't care who the president is.

00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:13.515
I don't care who the governor is.

00:01:13.515 --> 00:01:16.015
I don't care who the mayor is.

00:01:16.865 --> 00:01:18.907
My mama ain't counting on the governor.

00:01:18.907 --> 00:01:20.832
My wife ain't counting on the President

00:01:20.832 --> 00:01:22.264
of the United States of America.

00:01:22.264 --> 00:01:24.022
My wife ain't counting on the mayor.

00:01:24.022 --> 00:01:25.816
My wife ain't counting
on the commissioner.

00:01:25.816 --> 00:01:27.329
My wife counting on me.

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:29.622
When I walk out that
house, she's counting on me

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.291
to bring home the bacon.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.491
- I've never been a big fan
of things being handed to me.

00:01:33.491 --> 00:01:34.837
I've never enjoyed that.

00:01:34.837 --> 00:01:36.792
I've never liked, for whatever reason,

00:01:36.792 --> 00:01:37.935
it probably comes from my parents,

00:01:37.935 --> 00:01:40.427
of things just being handed to me

00:01:40.427 --> 00:01:42.180
without me having to earn it.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.492
I always felt like I wanted
to earn where I'm at.

00:01:45.492 --> 00:01:47.577
And so I come from a middle-class family.

00:01:47.577 --> 00:01:50.721
My parents had connections
that I could have really used

00:01:50.721 --> 00:01:52.382
when I was starting my business,

00:01:52.382 --> 00:01:54.517
but when I started my first company,

00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:56.433
I didn't use them at all.

00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:59.415
I wanted to prove to
myself that I could do it.

00:01:59.415 --> 00:02:02.562
I went to my banker and asked for advice

00:02:02.562 --> 00:02:03.908
and asked for help.

00:02:03.908 --> 00:02:06.606
That's how little I knew
about the business world.

00:02:06.606 --> 00:02:09.668
I walked into the bank and
said, "Hey, I'm trying to build

00:02:09.668 --> 00:02:12.036
a business, I could use some help".

00:02:12.036 --> 00:02:13.340
They asked if I needed a loan.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.421
I said I don't think I need a loan.

00:02:15.421 --> 00:02:17.085
I don't know, do I need a loan?

00:02:17.085 --> 00:02:19.778
They said well that's what banks do.

00:02:19.778 --> 00:02:23.389
That's how ignorant I
was about the process.

00:02:23.389 --> 00:02:25.292
But I didn't want to use
any of the connections

00:02:25.292 --> 00:02:27.989
my parents had, people that they knew

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:31.825
that could have springboarded
my business forward.

00:02:31.825 --> 00:02:34.464
If I look at now, I'm on
a personal training plan.

00:02:34.464 --> 00:02:36.801
I've got a personal trainer that comes in

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.928
a couple times a week
and trains me and Nina.

00:02:39.928 --> 00:02:44.091
Part of what he has us on
is a strict diet regiment.

00:02:44.091 --> 00:02:45.991
If we hit certain goals,

00:02:45.991 --> 00:02:48.290
then we get what he calls "re-feed days",

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.074
where we get to almost double
our calories for the day.

00:02:52.074 --> 00:02:54.032
We're excited, we've been eating lean,

00:02:54.032 --> 00:02:56.316
we've been preparing our
food, and we want to earn

00:02:56.316 --> 00:02:58.148
our re-feed days, and I tell him,

00:02:58.148 --> 00:03:00.110
Shawn, don't just give it to me.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.247
I need to earn it.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:04.751
As much as we want it, if I don't get it,

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.178
if I didn't hit the milestone,

00:03:06.178 --> 00:03:07.974
whatever you're looking
for in your criteria,

00:03:07.974 --> 00:03:09.735
don't do it because you
want to make me happy.

00:03:09.735 --> 00:03:11.609
Don't do it because you
like my YouTube channel.

00:03:11.609 --> 00:03:14.014
Don't do it for any other
reason except for the fact

00:03:14.014 --> 00:03:17.075
that I did the work, and I earned it.

00:03:17.075 --> 00:03:18.705
Because otherwise I don't want it.

00:03:18.705 --> 00:03:21.314
I will give up the weekend food day

00:03:21.314 --> 00:03:24.627
and continue to struggle until I get it.

00:03:24.627 --> 00:03:27.061
And it's just been my mindset.

00:03:27.061 --> 00:03:29.276
And I think it's really
helpful as an entrepreneur

00:03:29.276 --> 00:03:30.746
to have that kind of mindset.

00:03:30.746 --> 00:03:34.217
That you want to go out and
you want to earn your success.

00:03:34.217 --> 00:03:36.763
There's a lot of people who
look at successful people

00:03:36.763 --> 00:03:40.742
and they will complain that,
oh they had it handed to them,

00:03:40.742 --> 00:03:42.633
or somebody gave them a lucky break,

00:03:42.633 --> 00:03:44.453
or they got really lucky.

00:03:44.453 --> 00:03:46.374
If you look at the children of rich people

00:03:46.374 --> 00:03:47.718
and say well look at this person,

00:03:47.718 --> 00:03:49.878
they have it all made for
them, it's so easy for them.

00:03:49.878 --> 00:03:51.386
I feel bad for them.

00:03:51.386 --> 00:03:54.534
I feel bad for the kids
of really rich people.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.712
Show me the kid of a really rich person

00:03:57.712 --> 00:04:01.715
who went off and built an
amazing company on their own.

00:04:01.715 --> 00:04:04.648
It's not how it happens, they don't.

00:04:04.648 --> 00:04:07.301
The struggle is part of
what gives you the strength

00:04:07.301 --> 00:04:09.347
to go off and make amazing things.

00:04:09.347 --> 00:04:11.341
And so stop comparing
yourself to other people

00:04:11.341 --> 00:04:13.224
and say they have it, they've
had it handed to them,

00:04:13.224 --> 00:04:15.701
they grew up with this and that.

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.147
It doesn't matter.

00:04:17.147 --> 00:04:18.575
I think when you adopt that mentality,

00:04:18.575 --> 00:04:21.886
that you take responsibility
for where you are

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:24.820
and that you should earn
everything that you get,

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.246
that things shouldn't be handed to you,

00:04:26.246 --> 00:04:29.994
and they shouldn't be
handed to anybody else.

00:04:29.994 --> 00:04:34.126
When you fully believe that,
then you put in the work,

00:04:34.126 --> 00:04:36.673
then you don't expect handouts.

00:04:36.673 --> 00:04:38.223
Then you want to grind and hustle

00:04:38.223 --> 00:04:41.407
and get up every day and make
forward progress on your goal

00:04:41.407 --> 00:04:43.899
because nobody is coming to save you.

00:04:43.899 --> 00:04:46.636
Because there's no white
nag or no cavalry coming.

00:04:46.636 --> 00:04:48.879
It's on you to get it done.

00:04:48.879 --> 00:04:51.181
You need to earn your success.

00:04:51.181 --> 00:04:54.081
So the question of the day today is

00:04:54.081 --> 00:04:58.036
I'm curious, what are you
most proud of earning.

00:04:58.036 --> 00:05:02.112
You put in the work, and you
earned success for something.

00:05:02.112 --> 00:05:04.315
What are you most proud of?

00:05:04.315 --> 00:05:06.250
Leave that in the comments below.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.353
I'm really curious to find out.

00:05:07.353 --> 00:05:10.162
I also want to give a quick
shout out to William Chilton.

00:05:10.162 --> 00:05:11.881
William, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:11.881 --> 00:05:13.516
"Your One Word", and taking the picture

00:05:13.516 --> 00:05:16.781
and posting it to your Google Plus page.

00:05:16.781 --> 00:05:19.801
I really appreciate it
man, and I'm so glad

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:21.312
that you enjoyed the book.

00:05:21.312 --> 00:05:22.738
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:05:22.738 --> 00:05:25.666
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:28.157
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:28.157 --> 00:05:30.272
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:30.272 --> 00:05:32.840
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.825
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:35.825 --> 00:05:39.408
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:43.041 --> 00:05:47.208
- So when I was invited here
today, and they said "clever",

00:05:48.737 --> 00:05:52.717
I said to myself, hmm, I
don't think my approach

00:05:52.717 --> 00:05:56.884
in the industry that I am
in, the fitness industry,

00:05:58.831 --> 00:06:01.081
would be considered clever.

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:07.154
Because, in this day
and age and this time,

00:06:08.436 --> 00:06:12.353
it's a push or a trend
toward easier is better.

00:06:14.359 --> 00:06:17.168
The easier way, the easier approach.

00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:21.251
Five-minute abs, four-minute
abs, two-minute abs,

00:06:22.198 --> 00:06:26.196
one-minute abs (audience laughs).

00:06:26.196 --> 00:06:28.074
Now you're going to
think I'm making this up.

00:06:28.074 --> 00:06:31.574
But I seen an ad the other day for a belt.

00:06:32.724 --> 00:06:35.782
You just put it around your waistline,

00:06:35.782 --> 00:06:38.634
and you can sit on your
computer and watch Netflix,

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:41.840
chat with your boyfriend or girlfriend,

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:45.972
donkey or whatever it is you
talk to (audience laughs),

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:48.805
and it will work your abs for you.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:54.297
Wow, that's cool, I just sit there,

00:06:56.286 --> 00:06:59.752
and this machine will work my abs for me.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:03.919
I don't have to do one
sit-up, one crunch (mumbles).

00:07:04.855 --> 00:07:06.272
Not one, not one.

00:07:09.392 --> 00:07:13.559
And here I come along, old
crusty old man, 55 years old,

00:07:14.573 --> 00:07:17.188
and I look you in the eyeballs,

00:07:17.188 --> 00:07:19.479
point my finger in your face,

00:07:19.479 --> 00:07:23.623
and I say fuck that (audience laughs).

00:07:23.623 --> 00:07:26.422
Get your punk ass up off the couch

00:07:26.422 --> 00:07:29.172
and get down to that goddamn gym.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.484
And work for what you want.

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:35.708
I don't know if that will
be considered clever or not.

00:07:35.708 --> 00:07:37.776
What do you think?

00:07:37.776 --> 00:07:39.819
- My whole career has been
in some way or another

00:07:39.819 --> 00:07:43.493
a struggle against my own
doubts, all along the way.

00:07:43.493 --> 00:07:45.045
As much as people say
gosh, you're so confident,

00:07:45.045 --> 00:07:47.053
and you're the high-performance guy

00:07:47.053 --> 00:07:48.238
and everything else, and I'm like yeah,

00:07:48.238 --> 00:07:50.113
but it doesn't mean I don't struggle.

00:07:50.113 --> 00:07:52.803
As a matter of fact, I probably
put myself in situations

00:07:52.803 --> 00:07:56.651
where I must be challenged
and I must struggle

00:07:56.651 --> 00:07:59.299
more than any normal sane person.

00:07:59.299 --> 00:08:02.232
I'm constantly pushing
myself, all the time,

00:08:02.232 --> 00:08:06.313
because I evaluate struggle
as something to be honored.

00:08:06.313 --> 00:08:08.518
It used to be struggle was something

00:08:08.518 --> 00:08:11.002
that was truly honored by people.

00:08:11.002 --> 00:08:13.415
They thought that was
something that built character.

00:08:13.415 --> 00:08:15.370
They thought that was
something that was good.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.229
And now we've got to be such
a convenient-driven society

00:08:18.229 --> 00:08:21.893
that's into ease and
so much, just, I think,

00:08:21.893 --> 00:08:24.840
an unbelievable level of entitlement

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:27.117
where people don't think
they have to earn it.

00:08:27.117 --> 00:08:29.610
I was like wait, if you have a dream...

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:33.483
Never forget, if you knock
on the door of opportunity,

00:08:33.483 --> 00:08:35.792
that it is work who answers.

00:08:35.792 --> 00:08:38.529
It takes a lot of work to
achieve your bigger dreams,

00:08:38.529 --> 00:08:41.340
to become the best you who you can be,

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.053
to serve more, to create more,

00:08:43.053 --> 00:08:44.973
to contribute at the highest level.

00:08:44.973 --> 00:08:46.242
Man, it's a lot of work.

00:08:46.242 --> 00:08:49.131
- I didn't have an easy experience.

00:08:49.131 --> 00:08:52.450
I didn't come in as a top-rated recruit.

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:56.588
I didn't come in with the
opportunity to play right away.

00:08:56.588 --> 00:08:57.958
I had to earn it.

00:08:57.958 --> 00:09:00.501
And you know what the great
honor I've ever received

00:09:00.501 --> 00:09:01.751
as a player is?

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.451
In my fourth year and my fifth year,

00:09:05.451 --> 00:09:07.305
I was named team captain.

00:09:07.305 --> 00:09:11.439
That, to this day, is the
single greatest achievement

00:09:11.439 --> 00:09:14.295
I've ever had as a football player.

00:09:14.295 --> 00:09:18.318
Because the men in this room
chose me to lead their team.

00:09:18.318 --> 00:09:20.315
And these were my best friends.

00:09:20.315 --> 00:09:23.939
These were the guys that
knew that I liked to work,

00:09:23.939 --> 00:09:25.456
that knew that I love football,

00:09:25.456 --> 00:09:27.919
that knew that I love to play,

00:09:27.919 --> 00:09:32.057
that knew that I wanted to be
the quarterback for Michigan.

00:09:32.057 --> 00:09:35.625
And all the lessons that I
learned here on State Street,

00:09:35.625 --> 00:09:39.505
and in the big house,
that's still what I bring

00:09:39.505 --> 00:09:42.645
to practice today, and after 14 years,

00:09:42.645 --> 00:09:44.378
I love the game more
than I've ever loved it.

00:09:44.378 --> 00:09:46.414
But where did I learn
the love for the game?

00:09:46.414 --> 00:09:47.640
Where did I learn to practice?

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:49.683
Where did I learn to compete?

00:09:49.683 --> 00:09:52.056
It was sitting in the same chairs

00:09:52.056 --> 00:09:53.590
that you guys are sitting in today.

